{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_credit_at_subscription_start", "label": "Credit minted at subscription start, not checkout open", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Minting at checkout-open caused all three defects. Hanging off both the webhook and the reconcile-on-return arm is required, because wiring only the webhook silently drops the credit in exactly the environments where webhooks are not configured; the redemption row makes double-firing a no-op. Accepted regression: on the spent-trial path the credit now lands on invoice #2 instead of #1."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_credit_stacking_defect", "label": "Credit stacking / never expiring / surviving refund", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "Why", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All three reproduced against live Stripe test mode, not inferred. Five passes is \u00a3125 of credit \u2014 a free year of Pro \u2014 while the org keeps five competitions permanently upgraded. The refund case is ordinary support traffic and returns \u00a325 cash on top of \u00a325 already returned as credit, and it looks clean to support."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_pass_credit_redemptions_table", "label": "pass_credit_redemptions table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Group-keyed, with a partial unique index enforcing the lifetime cap in the database rather than in a Stripe balance-transaction scan (which is bounded to 1000 transactions, fails closed, and is invisible to support). The row survives deletion of the competition_passes row, which is what makes the refund path work at all."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_one_credit_per_group", "label": "One pass credit per billing group, ever", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "Product decisions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per group, not per org: a group is one Stripe customer, and a per-org cap would let a group collect \u00a325 per org it adds. A lifetime cap is a term of the offer, so every surface that promises the credit must state the limit \u2014 two currently imply the opposite."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_admin_pass_refund", "label": "Admin pass refund action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Computes cash_back = pass paid \u2212 (redeemed \u2212 unspent credit), so a fully consumed credit refunds nothing \u2014 the money already came back as Pro. Support refunds in the Stripe Dashboard, so the PaymentIntent is also stamped with 'redeemed as account credit' best-effort, since the warning has to live on the object they are looking at."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_charge_refunded_backstop", "label": "charge.refunded webhook backstop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dashboard refunds cannot be prevented, so the webhook reverses only the UNSPENT portion, idempotently, and never pushes the customer into debt \u2014 the consumed portion is absorbed and raises a staff alert, matching the rule recordPackRefund already follows for the AI wallet."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_credit_at_subscription_start", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_21_event_pass_and_entitlement_gaps_design_pass_to_pro_credit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "Status", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_credit_at_subscription_start", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_credit_stacking_defect", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_pass_credit_redemptions_table", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_one_credit_per_group", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_pass_credit_redemptions_table", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_21_billing_groups_design_billing_group", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_admin_pass_refund", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_pass_credit_redemptions_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "Phasing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_charge_refunded_backstop", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_pass_credit_redemptions_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_charge_refunded_backstop", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_21_billing_failure_paths_backlog_dispute_webhook_driven", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "event_pass_credit_money_model", "label": "Event Pass \u2192 Pro credit money model (mint, cap, reverse, refund)", "nodes": ["docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_21_event_pass_and_entitlement_gaps_design_pass_to_pro_credit", "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_credit_at_subscription_start", "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_pass_credit_redemptions_table", "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_one_credit_per_group", "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_charge_refunded_backstop", "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_pass_credit_redemption_design_admin_pass_refund"], "relation": "form", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-pass-credit-redemption-design.md"}]}